<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Rorke's Drift</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Rorke's Drift was fought on 22–23 January 1879 during the Anglo-Zulu War, when about 150 British soldiers defended a mission station on the Buffalo River against some 3,000–4,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> warriors, hours after the disaster at Isandlwana. The garrison held, and eleven Victoria Crosses were awarded. The defence was celebrated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and later in the film Zulu (1964).</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-rorkes-drift.jpg" alt="Battle of Rorke's Drift" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alphonse de Neuville · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alphonse_de_Neuville_-_The_defence_of_Rorke%27s_Drift_1879_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
